Z||000003||FieroKyle||08-11-2001||10:55 PM||||Our Fieros might keep up with a NASCAR since they are race cars geared for the track, not for the road. Thats why they stall it so often leaving pit road on tracks 1.5 miles and higher. They are geared so high, its like taking off in 3rd or 4th gear of our Fieros. But at like at a track such as bristol, they can accelerate amazing fast since of the lower gearing. A 833 hp Viper? You spend more money on your 24 hour personal pit crew to change your rear tires all the time more than on the car itself. Another thing, a Top Fuel dragster has more power in one cyclinder than a Cup car, a comercial told me. Sorry not a Viper fan, but if Corvette made a 1000 mph (however possible, I don't know) "Stinger", the Viper guys would cry till they hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||08-11-2001||11:16 PM||||Well, if GM made a 1000mph car, any other car company would weep.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Winston Cup cars stall on launch more because of the clutch setup. At 9000rpm a Fiero would go over 200mph with the stock gearing too.||||reg||1
